! Spirit Handback — the seat re-seals what stood before

Verbatim final message of the tasked spirit that closed the face-join pre-seat-binding gap (task `a3d865befef4a4aa1`, 2026-09-11), captured word-for-word with only Markdown transliterated to memetic-wikitext. Landed as commit `024210396`.

My work is complete. Here is the report.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-was-done>>

!! What was done

The hazard — ''"face-join never re-grants bindings minted vessel-only before the seat"'' — was real, but the measured root cause is deeper than the held canon recorded. I measured it against the ''real'' `KeyhiveProvider` (single booted provider reused — no second holder) and refined the ruling.

!!! The measurement (RED)

A probe against the real provider sealed a bag while the vessel stood ALONE, seated a member, then tried three strategies:

* ''Strategy A'' (no re-grant): decrypt rejects — the gap.
* ''Strategy B'' (re-delegate only — the ''currently committed'' `runFaceJoin` path): ''`DecryptError: Key not found`''. `regranted: 1` rides out, but the seated member reaches nothing.
* ''Strategy C'' (re-delegate + re-encrypt): reachable.

So the committed re-grant loop ''overclaimed'': `regranted` counted the re-pointed delegation, but keyhive reads FORWARD-ONLY — a re-delegate re-keys the bag forward and moves no already-sealed chunk. The codebase already knew this in `persona-crossing.ts` line 105: ''"route A owes a re-encrypt."'' face-join owed it and never paid it.

!!! The fix (GREEN)

# ''`keyhive-provider.ts`'' — the provider now tracks the latest ciphertext per (bag, contentRef) as it seals, and gains `reSealBag(bagUrl)`: decrypts each standing chunk with its own key and re-encrypts at the current epoch, returning the fresh ciphertext. Plaintext is transient — only ciphertext is ever held. (Also renamed the now-simpler `changeIdForContent` -> `contentRefBytes`.)
# ''`face-join.ts`'' — the re-grant loop, after each `delegate`, calls the optional `provider.reSealBag`; the grant now carries a `reSealed` field (the fresh chunks, base64) so the joinee ingests reachable ciphertext. The `regranted` doc comment is corrected to state the invariant: a re-delegate confers FORWARD reach only; pre-seat chunks need `reSealed`.
# ''`operator-daemon-behavior.ts`'' (face-join grant path only) — the daemon `joinProvider` wires `reSealBag` to the vessel provider (the holder that sealed the content and holds bag admin).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/tests>>

!! Tests

* ''`packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/pre-seat-reach.test.ts`'' (new, real provider):
** pre-seat sealed bag -> seat via `runFaceJoin` with re-grant -> member reaches it through the grant's `reSealed` chunk (green); original pre-seat bytes still reject `/key not found/` (documents ''why'' re-seal is needed).
** ''REGRESSION GUARD'': a pre-seat bag left OUT of the re-grant -> `reSealed: []`, member reads Key-not-found (the gap direction).
** ''CONTROL'': content sealed AFTER the seat reaches the member with NO re-seal — proving the fix targets backward-propagation only, not a blanket re-grant.

<<~/ahu>>

