<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/commit-message>>

!! Proposed commit message

```
lar:///the-seat.re-seals.what-stood-before — face-join re-encrypts pre-seat chunks, not just re-delegates

A bag sealed while the vessel stood alone stayed Key-not-found for a member seated
after it: keyhive reads forward-only, so the committed re-delegate re-keyed the bag
forward and moved no already-sealed chunk while regranted rode out looking healthy.
The provider now tracks its sealed chunks and re-seals them at the re-keyed epoch;
runFaceJoin carries the fresh ciphertext out on the grant; the daemon join path wires
the vessel as the re-seal holder. RED measured on the real provider (DecryptError:
Key not found under re-delegate-only), green with the re-seal, control proves post-seat
content still reaches with no re-seal.
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/deferred>>

!! Deferred (and why)

* ''Joinee-side ingestion of `reSealed` into the content plane'': the fix ships the re-sealed ciphertext on the grant and proves the member decrypts it, but the daemon face-join client's absorption of those chunks into the joinee's bag docs (Automerge/residency) is content-plane work outside the keyhive lane — not wired or asserted here.
* ''Veil->group transitive reach in the daemon path'': my green proof uses the direct pattern (seat holds the group, as in leaf-fleet-admit). The daemon re-seals on the vessel whose bag membership is the veil; whether the veil->group->joinee chain propagates the re-sealed epoch is the same forward-only question one hop up, and I did not stand a daemon integration test for it. The wiring strictly improves on re-delegate-only and cannot corrupt ciphertext (it re-seals to the same audience the original sealing used), but its end-to-end reach is unproven here.
* ''Canon refinement (worth a hoike/memory update)'': held canon says a pre-seat bag ''"needs a RE-DELEGATE."'' Measured: a re-delegate is necessary but NOT sufficient — the pre-seat CONTENT also needs a RE-SEAL. I did not edit memory files (dirty-tree discipline); flagging for the conductor.

I did not commit.

<<~/ahu>>

